WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
And so

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Basically, the idea of projects being bets is

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
It's kind of a bit like this

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:21.000
So, I don't know if you're familiar with Damon Runyon. He's the guy who wrote the stories that became Guys and Dolls, the musical

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.000
And

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:53.000
This is a quote from him. I long ago came to the conclusion that all life is six to five against. So I'm not a betting man, so I had to look up what six to five against meant

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
And a lot of behavior that we see around projects

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Is connected with the fact that

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:21.000
We don't really want to acknowledge that. We don't really want to kind of pretend that there's a possibility to not pretend. We want to pretend there's no possibility of the project failing. We want to rather

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Imagine that the project is going to always succeed.

